<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>
<i>Phase 2 gear into Phase 3</i></b>
<br/>It's no secret that <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4273/ulduar">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Ulduar</span></a> gear is great, it saw a <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/news/wowhead-wrath-classic-database-updated-item-levels-330095">major gear overhaul</a>, which goes a long way to carry it into phase 3. Even 10-man hardmode gear retains a lot of viability as it is afforded additional socket slots, making it competitive with 245 gear. This means that baseline you can expect all HM gear in <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4273/ulduar">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Ulduar</span></a> to be at the very least competitive with 25-man normal and 10-man heroic pieces in Phase 3. You can keep Ulduar 252 item level items around for a long time going into <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4722/trial-of-the-crusader">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Trial of the Crusader</span></a>. As it stands, none of the non-heroic tier pieces are worth chasing if you enter this phase with Ulduar BiS gear. However if you are still lacking critical items from Ulduar, we suggest that you upgrade your gear on an item level basis, replacing the lowest item level first. Following that, replace all block rating gear that you currently equip in Ulduar, target hit cap and as much stamina as you can get.</div></li></ul>
<ul>
<li class="fa fa-question">
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>
<i>Class token discussion part 2</i></b>
<br/>This phase is not known for its debilitating tank damage or being particularly challenging on healers, making it a really good building off point to prepare your DPS players for the more challenging content ahead in the next phase.  Because of this we advise you to de-prioritize yourself as much as possible, since as a tank you will have a hard time utilizing the stats you're given in an environment that won't challenge your survivability.<br/>
<br/>The only tier set that has items that are best in slot for this phase is the Heroic 25-man tier which sits at 258 item level, and can only be acquired if you can complete a full 25-man heroic. The abundance of these tokens are also scaling with how many attempts you have done in that raid, you will always get 2 tier (of any kind) tokens for clearing the raid on heroic, but on top of that 2 additional tokens will drop if you beat the raid at +45 attempts remaining.</div></li></ul>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="gems">Gems</h4>When gemming, you will want to use these slots to balance out your hit, expertise, defense, and match your meta gem requirement. Most often it is not worthwhile to get the gem bonus unless it is a +6 stamina per gem invested for the bonus. For more in-depth info on gems, see the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/guide/classes/paladin/protection/tank-enchants-gems-pve">Gem Guide.</a>
