<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="emblems">Emblems of Triumph for Protection Paladin Tank Phase 3</h3>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47241/emblem-of-triumph">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_summonchampion.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Triumph</span></a> is the new raid currency introduced in Phase 3, this is obtainable through 10 and 25-man Onyxia &amp; Trial of the Grand Crusader, as well as the daily heroic dungeon quest from <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=20735/archmage-landalock">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Archmage Lan'dalock</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>All gear from the Triumph vendor is iLevel-245 and may find themselves being passed over for a lot of players, existing in a place between Ulduar gear and Heroic pieces. For the most part these items are upgrades from Ulduar, however since the cost is high, thus time to acquire them high you might never wear any of them.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47661/libram-of-valiance">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_relics_libramofhope.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Libram of Valiance</span></a> is a solid DPS oriented upgrade, we list it very high because in terms of what you get for what you pay for this is the highest impact emblem piece. That said however this primarily applies to those that are full or near-bis from the previous phase and can readily afford to drop survivability for higher DPS.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47699/shoulderguards-of-enduring-order">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_shoulder_62.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shoulderguards of Enduring Order</span></a> &amp; <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47678/headplate-of-the-honorbound">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_98.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Headplate of the Honorbound</span></a> are definitive upgrades from Ulduar, these piece primarily compete with the 25-man normal tier shoulders. However while they might carry stronger stats, these could break your tier set bonuses so users beware.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47731/clutch-of-fortification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_50naxxramas.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Clutch of Fortification</span></a> is effectively a 245 version of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45112/the-leviathans-coil">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_71.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">The Leviathan's Coil</span></a>, though there is no shortage of strong rings in ToGC this is a good ring that you might wanna pick up at some point.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47735/glyph-of-indomitability">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_spiritshard_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Glyph of Indomitability</span></a> sits somewhere between <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45158/heart-of-iron">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_spiritshard_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heart of Iron</span></a>, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46021/royal-seal-of-king-llane">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_crown_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Royal Seal of King Llane</span></a> versus physical damage. While never say never there is a prominent increase in magic damage from this point on. This is primarily a catch-up item for those that never got their hands on anything better as we try to wear stamina over armor in all cases.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47734/mark-of-supremacy">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_bloodstone_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mark of Supremacy</span></a> &amp; <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=48722/shard-of-the-crystal-heart">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_spiritshard_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shard of the Crystal Heart</span></a> we quite like hit trinkets if we can afford to budget for it. The distinction of these trinkets are very narrow, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=48722/shard-of-the-crystal-heart">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_spiritshard_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shard of the Crystal Heart</span></a> pulls ahead on very short encounters.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47556/crusader-orb">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_rune.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Crusader Orb</span></a> could be a solid pick up if none of the above are interesting to you. These are used to craft <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47592/breastplate-of-the-white-knight">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate20.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Breastplate of the White Knight</span></a> &amp; <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47571/saronite-swordbreakers">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_30b.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Saronite Swordbreakers</span></a>, the latter is a near-bis/<wbr/>tech option in full bis.<br/>
<br/>The normal 10 man version tier of this phase is purchased with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47241/emblem-of-triumph">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_summonchampion.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Triumph</span></a>. The normal 25 man version also requires <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47242/trophy-of-the-crusade">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_trophy_argent.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Trophy of the Crusade</span></a>, if trophies are accessible to you we suggest that you target tier and upgrade using tier in respect to what is the biggest item level upgrade. However the set bonus is not that outstanding with the exception of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=48660/liadrins-legguards-of-triumph">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_plate_30.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Liadrin's Legguards of Triumph</span></a>, which can be key to hit capping this phase though note that hit is very abundant outside of the BiS gear that this might be completely superfluous to you while still gearing in phase 3. The only other reason to gun for tier this phase is to get the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=67187/item-paladin-t9-tank-4p-bonus">4-set bonus</a>. Getting this <b>may</b> enable you to plan your CDs better and get stronger mileage out of this spell though since many protection paladins go entire raids without using this skill, it's not for everyone.<br/>
<br/>
