<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="waist">Waist for Protection Paladin Tank Phase 3</h3>All the belts are just linear upgrades from each other in most respects. There is not much nuance to talk about, you'll wear what you have access to. The exception is that <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45241/belt-of-colossal-rage">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_49c.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Belt of Colossal Rage</span></a> is a very strong DPS belt, while the gap isn't as wide as it was in phase 2, there is certainly incentive to try and pick one of these up for those fights where your survivability is not prime concern.<div class="box">
<b>Waist Enchants</b>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=41611/eternal-belt-buckle">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_36.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Eternal Belt Buckle</span></a> is a universal item enhancement for your belt. <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/skill=202/engineering">Engineers</a> also get access to a <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=54793/frag-belt">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Frag Belt</span></a>.</div>
