<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="rings">Rings for Protection Paladin Tank Phase 3</h3>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47476/band-of-the-traitor-king">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_57.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Band of the Traitor King</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45471/fates-clutch">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_69.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fate's Clutch</span></a> is your BiS tanking ring setup for Phase 3. Fate's Clutch offers a slightly balanced advantage over <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=48027/band-of-the-twin-valkyr">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_59.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Band of the Twin Val'kyr</span></a> which is otherwise the runner up. Though if you're gearing exclusively for and from phase 3, adventuring for Fate's Clutch is not advisable, there are better things you could do with your time.<br/>
<br/>Boy I sure hope you like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45112/the-leviathans-coil">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_71.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">The Leviathan's Coil</span></a> because Blizzard decided to copy this item 2 times; <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47731/clutch-of-fortification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_50naxxramas.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Clutch of Fortification</span></a> &amp; <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47888/band-of-the-twin-valkyr">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_59.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Band of the Twin Val'kyr</span></a>. Item level is king here and you'll use these rings just as you'd use Leviathan's in phase 2.<br/>
<br/>With the Daughter of Deathwing returning <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=10184/onyxia">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Onyxia</span></a> she brings us many gifts for us. Not only a helmet, trinket she also has some pretty neat rings: <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49489/signified-ring-of-binding">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Signified Ring of Binding</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49309/runed-ring-of-binding">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Runed Ring of Binding</span></a>. Their design is nigh perfect for heroic 25-man <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=34564/anubarak">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Anub'arak</span></a>. Resistance on this fight has a major impact in the last phase of this fight where the boss will deal damage to the entire raid and heal himself for the damage dealt, as such resistance on these can mean not only the difference between life and death in terms of damage you take, but also drastically reduce the amount of healing you generate on the boss. These rings drop in 25m and 10m respectively.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45534/seal-of-the-betrayed-king">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_76.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Seal of the Betrayed King</span></a> is a very strong DPS ring, with phase 2 over we don't feel as bad for recommending that you ought to maybe pick one of these up if you have a good use-case for it. If you can't get it <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45540/bladebearers-signet">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_72.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bladebearer's Signet</span></a> is a decent consolation price, it's straight up worse but still worth getting as a DPS option.<div class="box">
<b>Ring Enchants</b>: <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=59636/enchant-ring-stamina">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engraving.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Ring - Stamina</span></a> -  Only Enchanters may apply Ring Enchants on their own rings.</div>
